# EXPERIMENT NAME

Testing Authentication Weaknesses and Session Management using Kali Linux and DVWA

---

# AIM

To identify and analyze authentication weaknesses and session management vulnerabilities in DVWA using Kali Linux, and to understand how improper authentication and insecure session handling can lead to unauthorized access.

---

# REQUIREMENTS

## Software

* Kali Linux
* DVWA (Damn Vulnerable Web Application)
* Firefox Browser
* Apache Server
* MySQL/MariaDB

## Hardware

* Computer System
* Lab Environment with Internet Disabled

---

# THEORY

## Authentication Weakness

Authentication ensures that only authorized users can access the system. Weak authentication occurs because of:

* Weak passwords
* Default credentials
* No account lockout
* Unlimited login attempts
* Brute force vulnerability

---

## Session Management

Session management maintains user identity using session IDs stored in cookies.

Improper session handling may cause:

* Session hijacking
* Session fixation
* Session reuse
* Insecure cookies
* Unauthorized access

