# RESULT

Authentication and session management vulnerabilities were successfully identified and analyzed in DVWA using Kali Linux. Weak authentication controls, brute force vulnerability, session hijacking, session fixation, and improper logout handling were demonstrated successfully.

---

# CONCLUSION

This experiment demonstrated that weak authentication mechanisms and insecure session management can lead to unauthorized access and account compromise. Proper password policies, session regeneration, secure cookie handling, account lockout mechanisms, and proper logout implementation are necessary to protect web applications against authentication and session-based attacks.

---

# PREVENTION TECHNIQUES

1. Strong Password Policies
2. Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)
3. Account Lockout Mechanisms
4. Secure Session ID Generation
5. Session Regeneration after Login
6. Secure and HttpOnly Cookies
7. Session Timeout
8. Proper Logout Session Destruction
9. Use HTTPS for Secure Communication

